              text: 'Is it the first thing that catches your attention? Do your eyes move across the layout in the order of priority you have planned? Step Take an A3 sheet and draw a cm margin on all four sides. Measure and draw parallel lines that will guide you in writing words in a straight line. Step Draw the visuals, add details, and colour the poster. ACTIVITY 5.1 c reate Y our P oster Use the principles of emphasis and hierarchy to create your poster. Step Choose a message you want to communicate to your friends. For example, classroom cleanliness, road safety, or everyday hygiene. Step Plan the images you want to include and decide what size each one should be. Step Write a phrase or sentence for your message. Ask your teacher to help you check the grammar and spelling. Step Plan the hierarchy (the order of priority) for the images and text. Decide the most important to the least important elements.   Part-1 Part-1 Visual Arts Create the rough layout of your poster here. Part-1 Part-1 Bansuri • Grade Design principles are not only used in posters but also in advertisements. Gather old newspapers or magazines and cut out small advertisements and paste them here. Observe the emphasis and order of importance in the design and mark them. Part-1 Part-1 Visual Arts Assessment – SPREADING THE MESSAGE CG C Learning Outcomes Teacher Self C–1.1 Creates posters that address issues and events in everyday life. C–2.1 Uses the design principles while making posters. C–3.2 Considers different contexts for making posters and plans work accordingly. Overall participation in class.',
